# Use an imperative, capitalized subject line without a period.
# It should complete: "If applied, this commit will <subject>."
# Keep the subject at 72 characters or fewer.

# Explain what changed and why when a body is useful. Wrap body lines at
# 72 characters. Do not describe implementation details the diff shows.
# Include the original problem, how the change addresses it, and any effects
# or known limitations. State the original issue for the reviewer.
# Do not include comments specific to a patch set.

# Add issue references in the body when applicable, for example:
# Fixes #123